    "title": "Health Check-Up Camp",
    "date": "21st September 2025",
    "summary": "Health Check-Up Camp",
    "content": "Women's Health Initiative: Building Stronger Communities Through Care\n\nHonoring Service Through Healthcare\n\nDuring Sewa Parv—a national celebration of service, creativity, and cultural heritage—Unnat Bharat Abhiyan (UBA) collaborated with NSS IIT Bhubaneswar, Sanjeevan Health Center, and the Literacy Mission to conduct a comprehensive Health Check-up Camp on Sunday, September 21, 2025, at Lalitgiri Hall of Learning (L12M).\n\nHealthy Women, Strong Families\n\nThe initiative embraced the theme 'Swasth Nari, Sashakt Parivar Abhiyaan' (Healthy Women, Empowered Families), acknowledging that women's wellness creates the foundation for thriving households and resilient communities. The camp welcomed migrant workers' families and sanitation staff, providing fair healthcare access throughout the institute community.\n\nMajor Accomplishments\n\n• More than 100 participants, primarily women construction workers, received quality medical care\n• Full services provided complimentary blood tests, health assessments, and necessary medications\n• Skilled medical professionals from Sanjeevan Health Center performed comprehensive examinations with caring attention\n• Over 100 committed NSS volunteers ensured smooth operations through participant assistance, coordination, and health education\n• Refreshments offered comfort and warm hospitality to all participants\n\nEnduring Benefits\n\nThe drive went beyond treating current health issues to highlight the critical importance of preventive healthcare for women. It strengthened the essential understanding that healthy women create strong families and thriving communities.\n\nThe sincere involvement of workers paired with dedicated NSS volunteer service demonstrated community compassion and unity in action.\n\nAcknowledgments\n\nThis meaningful initiative was accomplished under Dr. Madhusmita Dash's leadership (UBA Coordinator; Assistant Professor, SHSSM, IIT Bhubaneswar), through the combined work of UBA, NSS IIT Bhubaneswar, Sanjeevan Health Center, and the Literacy Mission. Together, these teams captured the spirit of Sewa Parv and advanced the vision of Viksit Bharat 2047.\n\nNot Me, But You.\nNSS, IITBBS",
