    "title": "Nutrition and Wellbeing Camp",
    "date": "14th September 2025",
    "summary": "Nutrition and Wellbeing Camp",
    "content": "Eat Smart, Stay Strong: A Journey to Better Nutrition\n\nStarting the Conversation\nWhat should we eat? What should we avoid? This fundamental question launched today's NSS nutrition and well-being event, held as part of Poshan Maah celebrations at IIT Bhubaneswar. In our fast-paced lives, convenience foods often replace nutritious meals, but this session emphasized that genuine health begins in the kitchen, not the hospital.\n\nThe program focused on building awareness about conscious eating, particularly among young people who frequently neglect balanced nutrition. It provided students with an opportunity to examine their daily eating patterns, ask questions, and discover practical improvement strategies.\n\nKey Session Features\nDr. Anjana Tripathy, Visiting Clinical Nutritionist, led the session with valuable guidance on healthy eating habits. Many students revealed they skip breakfast, which she identified as one of young people's most significant nutritional errors. Breakfast energizes both body and mind, and missing it diminishes energy levels and concentration.\n\nThe presentation was highly participatory, with students discussing their eating behaviors and concerns while Dr. Tripathy offered straightforward, practical advice. To maintain engagement, participants sampled delicious yet nutritious snacks, demonstrating that healthy eating and great taste complement each other perfectly.\n\nA crucial message was directed to young women: \\\"Eat more, eat right.\\\" Food restriction is never the answer. True strength and development come from balanced meals featuring fruits, vegetables, milk, nuts, pulses, and nourishing home-prepared food.\n\nWrapping Up\nThe session ended with a powerful reminder: Skipping meals is never trendy. Balanced eating is the wisest investment in your future.\n\nWith 130 students in attendance, NSS expresses sincere appreciation to our faculty coordinators for their ongoing support and to all engaged participants who made this program valuable.\n\nNot Me but You\nNSS, IITBBS",
