    "title": "Bridging Cultures: NSS Odia Learning Sessions at IIT Bhubaneswar",
    "date": "16th August to 4th September",
    "summary": "NSS Odia Learning Sessions at IIT Bhubaneswar",
    "content": "Language is more than just words—it is a bridge to connect hearts and communities. To help the new NSS volunteers at IIT Bhubaneswar engage better with local people and nearby schools, Odia learning sessions were organized under the guidance of our NSS teacher Dr. Sivaiah Bathula from 18th August to 3rd September 2025, every evening in the interactive classrooms of Lalitgiri Hall of Learning (LHL).\n\nWhat began with mixed feelings soon turned into a wholesome journey. Some volunteers thought, \"Why should I learn another language?\" while others were nervous about pronunciation. A few were excited to pick up something new. Very soon, the classroom became a space full of curiosity, laughter, and learning. With about 100 NSS volunteers participating, the atmosphere was truly vibrant.\n\nAt the heart of these sessions was Dr. Satchidananda Rath, Associate Professor, Department of Physics. Despite his busy research in fields such as nanoclusters, semiconductors, and soft matter physics—and even holding the Japan Society for Promotion of Science award (2007)—he graciously agreed to guide us, without expecting any incentives. For us, he was not just a teacher but a mentor who patiently taught Odia \"like a father.\"\n\nThe classes were not just about grammar and vocabulary. We learned to write our names in Odia, count confidently, and even explore the cultural shades of the language. Sometimes, pronunciation turned hilarious, with the same word meaning different things in different languages. Odia volunteers helped their peers, while friends from Tamil Nadu, Telangana, Bihar, Madhya Pradesh, Assam, Manipur, Rajasthan, and West Bengal all joined hands to pick up new words. Many realized that Odia feels like a beautiful blend of Hindi and Bengali. These funny mix-ups and team efforts turned each session into a rollercoaster of emotions.\n\nThe highlight came on 4th September, when the NSS family celebrated Teachers' Day. With singing, dancing, anchoring, acting, and even calligraphy displays, the celebration reflected the creativity and spirit of the volunteers. Rath Sir, Sivaiah sir, seniors and coordinators shared heartfelt messages on the importance of teachers and their life experiences. But what made the day truly memorable was the effort of 5–10 NSS volunteers who prepared burgers for nearly 200 people, making the celebration unique and joyful.\n\nLooking back, the Odia sessions were more than just language classes. They were about cultural bonding, laughter, teamwork, and respect for teachers. Today, we can proudly say—we are not just NSS volunteers, but also learners who can confidently communicate in Odia.\n\nNSS IIT Bhubaneswar\n\"Not Me, But You.\"",
